{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRH9vXtFYws5xdJs4Gwu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0139tZn7pJ3ZyXmWc3aybFir","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-d0de10e622b0e2942987a4b9c044b402/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":633,"cache_read_input_tokens":23906,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":633},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"eee9af04-6a40-4c28-9902-2c528facd150","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:10:29.395Z","request_id":"req_011ChRH9vKjRfR523JKpsdxs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0139tZn7pJ3ZyXmWc3aybFir":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-d0de10e622b0e2942987a4b9c044b402/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0139tZn7pJ3ZyXmWc3aybFir","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tslug: pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout\n3\tstatus: in-progress        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\n4\tcreated_at: 2026-11-25\n5\tcompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\n6\tsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\n7\tdepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\n8\tremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\n9\tpriority: 2\n10\tcomponents: pose-mcp\n11\ttask_type: bugfix\n12\tsurface: standard\n13\tdelivers: capability:review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t# Spec: pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout\n17\t\n18\t## 1. Intent\n19\t\n20\t### Goal\n21\tMake `pose delegate resume` give the resumed reviewer session a sealed checkout it can reach: either at the path the interrupted run used, or with the new path stated to the session, so a resume never points the reviewer at a removed directory.\n22\t\n23\t### Business value\n24\tOn 2026-11-25 round 11 of `pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes` hit the Codex usage limit; `pose delegate resume rrn-7e7520ad4fac9345` started a new run whose session still referred to the first attempt's sealed checkout, which the cleanup had removed. The reviewer correctly stopped (`the sealed checkout ... has disappeared`), the resume produced no draft, and the round had to be dispatched again from scratch.\n25\t\n26\t### Constraints\n27\tThe resumed run still reviews exactly the sealed subject; no path outside the run's runtime is trusted.\n28\t\n29\t### Non-goals\n30\tChanging round accounting or the conclusion step.\n31\t\n32\t## 2. Requirements\n33\t\n34\t### Functional\n35\t- R1: A resumed run shall materialize its sealed checkout where the resumed session can reach it, or tell the session its new path in the continuation prompt.\n36\t- R2: A regression test shall resume an interrupted run whose first checkout was removed and see the session work in the recreated checkout.\n37\t- R3: The attempt's runtime directory shall be created exclusively: an existing path, a link included, shall fail the run with its reason, never be shared or followed; a resume beside it shall be refused before the continuation is claimed.\n38\t\n39\t### Non-functional\n40\tExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n41\t\n42\t### Security\n43\tNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n44\t\n45\t### Compatibility\n46\tRuns recorded by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n47\t\n48\t## 3. Technical Plan\n49\t\n50\t### Affected areas\n51\t`pose-mcp` review dispatch: the runtime directory of a run (`reviewRunRuntimeDir` in `internal/pose/review_dispatch.go`).\n52\t\n53\t### Artifacts\n54\t- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout.md\n55\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n56\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\n57\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go\n58\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n59\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\n60\t- modified: POSE.md\n61\t- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n62\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n63\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n64\t\n65\t### Delivery targets\n66\t- capability:review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n67\t\n68\t### Accepted limits\n69\t- L1: The path is derived from the temporary directory of the process that dispatches, so a resume run with another `TMPDIR` recreates the checkout elsewhere and the session meets the old failure. Accepted because the dispatcher's environment is the operator's and the failure is the same one this spec removes for the usual case, a resume from the same shell.\n70\t- L2: The path is predictable, so another local user can create it first and block the attempt's runs. Accepted because the directory is created exclusively and never followed, so such a path only fails the run with its reason and is never shared.\n71\t- L3: A process that escaped an earlier run of the attempt knows the next run's paths, including its output file outside the checkout, which random names used to hide. Accepted because such a process already runs as the dispatching user and can reach any of that user's paths; on Linux the review run shim ends the run's subtree, and elsewhere the escape is the limit `pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux` addresses.\n72\t\n73\t### API/contract changes\n74\tNone: the run records, briefs and adapter commands are unchanged; only where the run directory is created changes.\n75\t\n76\t### Data/storage changes\n77\tNone.\n78\t\n79\t### Technical risks\n80\tA run whose cleanup failed leaves the directory, and resume already refuses such a predecessor. A directory present although the last run cleaned up (another process holding the path) makes resume and handoff refuse before they claim the run, naming the directory, so removing it restores them; a run that fails before anything is in the directory removes it.\n81\t\n82\t## 4. Tasks\n83\t\n84\t### Planning\n85\t- [x] Confirm how the continuation prompt and the worktree path are built.\n86\t\n87\t### Implementation\n88\t- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n89\t\n90\t### Validation\n91\t- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n92\t\n93\t## 5. Decisions\n94\t\n95\t### Decision D1\n96\t- Basis: R1, R3\n97\tKeep the checkout where the session last saw it rather than telling the session a new path: the continuation sends the same sealed brief, whose wire digest the provenance checks, so adding a path notice would change what is verified; a path stable per attempt changes nothing the run records. Every run of an attempt uses `pose-review-run-<first 32 hex of the attempt id>` under the temporary directory, created exclusively; a run with no attempt keeps a random name.\n98\t\n99\t## 6. Validation\n100\t\n101\t### Strategy\n102\tEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n103\t\n104\t### Deterministic checks\n105\t\n106\t#### Test\n107\t- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n108\t\n109\t### Execution log\n110\t- 2026-11-26: `reviewRunRuntimeDir` gives every run of an attempt the same runtime directory, created with `os.Mkdir` (no link followed, an existing path refused). `TestResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath` fails with the random name restored (the session was moved from the first checkout); `TestTheAttemptRuntimeDirectoryIsCreatedExclusively` fails with `MkdirAll`.\n111\t- 2026-11-26: review round 1 (rrn-7adbffa551b9acf2, Claude Sonnet 5.5) ended without a draft: its Bash sandbox did not start. From its reading: N1, resume refuses a leftover runtime directory before claiming the continuation (the test fails with the check mutated out); N2, the R2 adapter fails unless the recreated checkout holds the spec; N3, the manual in both locales states the stable path, the `TMPDIR` condition and the remedy; N4, a run that fails right after creating the directory removes it; N5 is declared as L3.\n112\t- 2026-11-26: the full suite caught a repeated resume refused beside the directory; the check now runs only for a continuation still to start. Review round 2 (rrn-c5d57ff07d69ec1a) requested changes: N7, the manual, the technical risks and the messages no longer promise that removing a directory left by an unfinished cleanup restores resume (that predecessor is refused anyway); N6, a handoff checks the directory before it claims the run (the test fails with the check mutated out); N9, the regression tests are named `TestRunContinuity…`, so the matrix's continuity pattern runs them; N10, the exclusivity test isolates `TMP` and `TEMP` as well. N8 is a follow-up.\n113\t\n114\t### Results summary\n115\tThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n116\t\n117\t### Requirement trace\n118\t- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath\n119\t- R2 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath\n120\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityAttemptRuntimeDirectoryIsCreatedExclusively, test:TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath\n121\t\n122\t### Known gaps\n123\tNone.\n124\t\n125\t## 7. Final Report\n126\t\n127\t### Delivered scope\n128\tA resumed review run recreates its sealed checkout at the path the interrupted run used, so the resumed session keeps working in it.\n129\t\n130\t### Files and modules changed\n131\t`pose-mcp` review dispatch and its tests.\n132\t\n133\t### Validation executed\n134\t`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n135\t\n136\t### Residual risks\n137\tL1, L2 and L3 above.\n138\t\n139\t### Follow-ups\n140\t- [open] Make the continuation claim and the runtime-directory check one step, so a resume that loses a race is told the continuation is pending instead of being asked to remove a live run's directory (review round 2, N8). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n141\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"7c56cf23-061e-46b1-87f7-e349e730809f","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:10:29.404Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-d0de10e622b0e2942987a4b9c044b402/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout.md","content":"---\nslug: pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout\nstatus: in-progress        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\ncreated_at: 2026-11-25\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority: 2\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface: standard\ndelivers: capability:review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nMake `pose delegate resume` give the resumed reviewer session a sealed checkout it can reach: either at the path the interrupted run used, or with the new path stated to the session, so a resume never points the reviewer at a removed directory.\n\n### Business value\nOn 2026-11-25 round 11 of `pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes` hit the Codex usage limit; `pose delegate resume rrn-7e7520ad4fac9345` started a new run whose session still referred to the first attempt's sealed checkout, which the cleanup had removed. The reviewer correctly stopped (`the sealed checkout ... has disappeared`), the resume produced no draft, and the round had to be dispatched again from scratch.\n\n### Constraints\nThe resumed run still reviews exactly the sealed subject; no path outside the run's runtime is trusted.\n\n### Non-goals\nChanging round accounting or the conclusion step.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: A resumed run shall materialize its sealed checkout where the resumed session can reach it, or tell the session its new path in the continuation prompt.\n- R2: A regression test shall resume an interrupted run whose first checkout was removed and see the session work in the recreated checkout.\n- R3: The attempt's runtime directory shall be created exclusively: an existing path, a link included, shall fail the run with its reason, never be shared or followed; a resume beside it shall be refused before the continuation is claimed.\n\n### Non-functional\nExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n\n### Security\nNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n\n### Compatibility\nRuns recorded by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n`pose-mcp` review dispatch: the runtime directory of a run (`reviewRunRuntimeDir` in `internal/pose/review_dispatch.go`).\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\n- modified: POSE.md\n- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n\n### Delivery targets\n- capability:review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n\n### Accepted limits\n- L1: The path is derived from the temporary directory of the process that dispatches, so a resume run with another `TMPDIR` recreates the checkout elsewhere and the session meets the old failure. Accepted because the dispatcher's environment is the operator's and the failure is the same one this spec removes for the usual case, a resume from the same shell.\n- L2: The path is predictable, so another local user can create it first and block the attempt's runs. Accepted because the directory is created exclusively and never followed, so such a path only fails the run with its reason and is never shared.\n- L3: A process that escaped an earlier run of the attempt knows the next run's paths, including its output file outside the checkout, which random names used to hide. Accepted because such a process already runs as the dispatching user and can reach any of that user's paths; on Linux the review run shim ends the run's subtree, and elsewhere the escape is the limit `pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux` addresses.\n\n### API/contract changes\nNone: the run records, briefs and adapter commands are unchanged; only where the run directory is created changes.\n\n### Data/storage changes\nNone.\n\n### Technical risks\nA run whose cleanup failed leaves the directory, and resume already refuses such a predecessor. A directory present although the last run cleaned up (another process holding the path) makes resume and handoff refuse before they claim the run, naming the directory, so removing it restores them; a run that fails before anything is in the directory removes it.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Planning\n- [x] Confirm how the continuation prompt and the worktree path are built.\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n\n### Validation\n- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Basis: R1, R3\nKeep the checkout where the session last saw it rather than telling the session a new path: the continuation sends the same sealed brief, whose wire digest the provenance checks, so adding a path notice would change what is verified; a path stable per attempt changes nothing the run records. Every run of an attempt uses `pose-review-run-<first 32 hex of the attempt id>` under the temporary directory, created exclusively; a run with no attempt keeps a random name.\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Execution log\n- 2026-11-26: `reviewRunRuntimeDir` gives every run of an attempt the same runtime directory, created with `os.Mkdir` (no link followed, an existing path refused). `TestResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath` fails with the random name restored (the session was moved from the first checkout); `TestTheAttemptRuntimeDirectoryIsCreatedExclusively` fails with `MkdirAll`.\n- 2026-11-26: review round 1 (rrn-7adbffa551b9acf2, Claude Sonnet 5.5) ended without a draft: its Bash sandbox did not start. From its reading: N1, resume refuses a leftover runtime directory before claiming the continuation (the test fails with the check mutated out); N2, the R2 adapter fails unless the recreated checkout holds the spec; N3, the manual in both locales states the stable path, the `TMPDIR` condition and the remedy; N4, a run that fails right after creating the directory removes it; N5 is declared as L3.\n- 2026-11-26: the full suite caught a repeated resume refused beside the directory; the check now runs only for a continuation still to start. Review round 2 (rrn-c5d57ff07d69ec1a) requested changes: N7, the manual, the technical risks and the messages no longer promise that removing a directory left by an unfinished cleanup restores resume (that predecessor is refused anyway); N6, a handoff checks the directory before it claims the run (the test fails with the check mutated out); N9, the regression tests are named `TestRunContinuity…`, so the matrix's continuity pattern runs them; N10, the exclusivity test isolates `TMP` and `TEMP` as well. N8 is a follow-up.\n\n### Results summary\nThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityAttemptRuntimeDirectoryIsCreatedExclusively, test:TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath\n\n### Known gaps\nNone.\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nA resumed review run recreates its sealed checkout at the path the interrupted run used, so the resumed session keeps working in it.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n`pose-mcp` review dispatch and its tests.\n\n### Validation executed\n`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n\n### Residual risks\nL1, L2 and L3 above.\n\n### Follow-ups\n- [open] Make the continuation claim and the runtime-directory check one step, so a resume that loses a race is told the continuation is pending instead of being asked to remove a live run's directory (review round 2, N8). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n","numLines":141,"startLine":1,"totalLines":141}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0139tZn7pJ3ZyXmWc3aybFir","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
