{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AztQZt1KVnnk3yULGVVxed","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Clean-host package-manager install verification (spec\n2\t# pose-package-manager-distribution, R3): installs the real published\n3\t# release through the generated Homebrew formula and WinGet manifest on\n4\t# unmodified macOS and Windows runners — no shared state with the release\n5\t# job, no local build shortcuts — then exercises the installed binary.\n6\tname: Package channels\n7\ton:\n8\t  # Deferred native verification: dispatch only after implementation is complete.\n9\t  # This optional round does not gate implementation, PRs or release publication.\n10\t  workflow_dispatch:\n11\t    inputs:\n12\t      tag:\n13\t        description: \"Release tag to verify (vX.Y.Z)\"\n14\t        required: true\n15\tpermissions: { contents: read }\n16\tjobs:\n17\t  package-channels:\n18\t    strategy:\n19\t      fail-fast: false\n20\t      matrix:\n21\t        os: [macos-latest, windows-latest]\n22\t    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}\n23\t    steps:\n24\t      # Validate the manually supplied tag before using it as a checkout ref.\n25\t      - name: Resolve the release tag\n26\t        shell: bash\n27\t        env:\n28\t          RAW_REF: ${{ inputs.tag }}\n29\t        run: |\n30\t          set -euo pipefail\n31\t          case \"$RAW_REF\" in\n32\t            v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*) ;;\n33\t            *) echo \"refusing to build channels for a ref that is not a release tag: $RAW_REF\" >&2; exit 1 ;;\n34\t          esac\n35\t          echo \"RELEASE_TAG=$RAW_REF\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n36\t      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1\n37\t      - name: Check out the release tag\n38\t        shell: bash\n39\t        run: |\n40\t          set -euo pipefail\n41\t          git fetch --depth 1 origin \"refs/tags/$RELEASE_TAG:refs/tags/$RELEASE_TAG\"\n42\t          git checkout --detach \"refs/tags/$RELEASE_TAG\"\n43\t      - uses: actions/setup-go@b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e # v7.0.0\n44\t        with:\n45\t          go-version: \"1.26.11\"\n46\t          cache: false\n47\t      - name: Download release checksums\n48\t        shell: bash\n49\t        env:\n50\t          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n51\t          REPO: ${{ github.repository }}\n52\t        run: gh release download \"$RELEASE_TAG\" --repo \"$REPO\" --pattern checksums.txt\n53\t      - name: Generate package-manager manifests\n54\t        shell: bash\n55\t        run: |\n56\t          set -euo pipefail\n57\t          # The Go module lives in pose-mcp/, not at the repository root: the\n58\t          # previous form failed in 26s on both runners with \"cannot find main\n59\t          # module\" the one time this gate was ever dispatched.\n60\t          go -C pose-mcp run ./cmd/pose release-package-manifests \\\n61\t            --version \"${RELEASE_TAG#v}\" \\\n62\t            --checksums ../checksums.txt \\\n63\t            --out ../package-manifests\n64\t      - name: Install via Homebrew\n65\t        if: runner.os == 'macOS'\n66\t        shell: bash\n67\t        # Homebrew rejects a formula that is not in a tap — installing from a\n68\t        # path or a URL is no longer supported, and HOMEBREW_DEVELOPER is\n69\t        # explicitly unsupported too. The formula therefore goes into a\n70\t        # throwaway local tap, which is the same shape a published tap has, so\n71\t        # the gate exercises the formula the release actually ships\n72\t        # (spec pose-package-channel-install-repair).\n73\t        run: |\n74\t          set -euo pipefail\n75\t          brew tap-new --no-git harne8/local\n76\t          tap=\"$(brew --repository harne8/local)\"\n77\t          mkdir -p \"$tap/Formula\"\n78\t          cp package-manifests/homebrew/pose.rb \"$tap/Formula/pose.rb\"\n79\t          brew install --formula harne8/local/pose\n80\t          smoke=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n81\t          git -C \"$smoke\" init -q\n82\t          pose install \"$smoke\" --skip-mcp\n83\t          (cd \"$smoke\" && pose doctor --json)\n84\t          brew uninstall pose\n85\t      - name: Install via WinGet\n86\t        if: runner.os == 'Windows'\n87\t        shell: pwsh\n88\t        # Installing from a local manifest is off by default and has to be\n89\t        # enabled by an administrator; without it winget prints its help and\n90\t        # exits 1, which reads like a usage error rather than a disabled\n91\t        # feature (spec pose-package-channel-install-repair).\n92\t        run: |\n93\t          winget settings --enable LocalManifestFiles\n94\t          # The msstore source demands its own agreements even for an install\n95\t          # that never touches it, and cancels the operation after the download\n96\t          # has already succeeded. This install reads a local manifest, so the\n97\t          # source is removed rather than agreed to.\n98\t          winget source remove --name msstore\n99\t          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { Write-Host \"msstore source already absent\" }\n100\t          $global:LASTEXITCODE = 0\n101\t\n102\t          # Each guarantee is asserted on its own, so a failure names which one\n103\t          # broke rather than surfacing as the step's last exit code.\n104\t          winget validate --manifest .\\package-manifests\\winget\n105\t          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"manifest set failed winget validation\" }\n106\t\n107\t          winget install --manifest .\\package-manifests\\winget --accept-package-agreements --accept-source-agreements --disable-interactivity\n108\t          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"install from the published manifest failed\" }\n109\t\n110\t          # The source checkout's project state is unrelated to the installed\n111\t          # binary and may differ after a Windows checkout. Inspect a fresh\n112\t          # instance created by that binary instead.\n113\t          $smoke = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP \"pose-package-channel-smoke\"\n114\t          New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $smoke | Out-Null\n115\t          git -C $smoke init -q\n116\t          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"could not initialize the smoke repository\" }\n117\t          pose install $smoke --skip-mcp\n118\t          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"the installed binary could not install a fresh instance\" }\n119\t          Push-Location $smoke\n120\t          try {\n121\t            pose doctor --json\n122\t            if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"the installed binary failed doctor in a fresh instance\" }\n123\t          } finally {\n124\t            Pop-Location\n125\t          }\n126\t\n127\t          # Cleanup, not a guarantee: winget does not track an archive package\n128\t          # installed from a local manifest, so neither --id nor --manifest\n129\t          # resolves it afterwards and it reports \"no installed package found\"\n130\t          # straight after a successful install. The runner is ephemeral, so\n131\t          # this is tolerated rather than allowed to fail the channel claim.\n132\t          winget uninstall --manifest .\\package-manifests\\winget --disable-interactivity\n133\t          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { Write-Host \"note: locally-installed archive package is not resolvable for uninstall; skipping cleanup\" }\n134\t          $global:LASTEXITCODE = 0\n135\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"cbf0c083-fd14-4029-b2f6-8fc6208e2c95","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:11:36.353Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-d0de10e622b0e2942987a4b9c044b402/worktree/.github/workflows/package-channels.yml","content":"# Clean-host package-manager install verification (spec\n# pose-package-manager-distribution, R3): installs the real published\n# release through the generated Homebrew formula and WinGet manifest on\n# unmodified macOS and Windows runners — no shared state with the release\n# job, no local build shortcuts — then exercises the installed binary.\nname: Package channels\non:\n  # Deferred native verification: dispatch only after implementation is complete.\n  # This optional round does not gate implementation, PRs or release publication.\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      tag:\n        description: \"Release tag to verify (vX.Y.Z)\"\n        required: true\npermissions: { contents: read }\njobs:\n  package-channels:\n    strategy:\n      fail-fast: false\n      matrix:\n        os: [macos-latest, windows-latest]\n    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}\n    steps:\n      # Validate the manually supplied tag before using it as a checkout ref.\n      - name: Resolve the release tag\n        shell: bash\n        env:\n          RAW_REF: ${{ inputs.tag }}\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          case \"$RAW_REF\" in\n            v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*) ;;\n            *) echo \"refusing to build channels for a ref that is not a release tag: $RAW_REF\" >&2; exit 1 ;;\n          esac\n          echo \"RELEASE_TAG=$RAW_REF\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1\n      - name: Check out the release tag\n        shell: bash\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          git fetch --depth 1 origin \"refs/tags/$RELEASE_TAG:refs/tags/$RELEASE_TAG\"\n          git checkout --detach \"refs/tags/$RELEASE_TAG\"\n      - uses: actions/setup-go@b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e # v7.0.0\n        with:\n          go-version: \"1.26.11\"\n          cache: false\n      - name: Download release checksums\n        shell: bash\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          REPO: ${{ github.repository }}\n        run: gh release download \"$RELEASE_TAG\" --repo \"$REPO\" --pattern checksums.txt\n      - name: Generate package-manager manifests\n        shell: bash\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          # The Go module lives in pose-mcp/, not at the repository root: the\n          # previous form failed in 26s on both runners with \"cannot find main\n          # module\" the one time this gate was ever dispatched.\n          go -C pose-mcp run ./cmd/pose release-package-manifests \\\n            --version \"${RELEASE_TAG#v}\" \\\n            --checksums ../checksums.txt \\\n            --out ../package-manifests\n      - name: Install via Homebrew\n        if: runner.os == 'macOS'\n        shell: bash\n        # Homebrew rejects a formula that is not in a tap — installing from a\n        # path or a URL is no longer supported, and HOMEBREW_DEVELOPER is\n        # explicitly unsupported too. The formula therefore goes into a\n        # throwaway local tap, which is the same shape a published tap has, so\n        # the gate exercises the formula the release actually ships\n        # (spec pose-package-channel-install-repair).\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          brew tap-new --no-git harne8/local\n          tap=\"$(brew --repository harne8/local)\"\n          mkdir -p \"$tap/Formula\"\n          cp package-manifests/homebrew/pose.rb \"$tap/Formula/pose.rb\"\n          brew install --formula harne8/local/pose\n          smoke=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n          git -C \"$smoke\" init -q\n          pose install \"$smoke\" --skip-mcp\n          (cd \"$smoke\" && pose doctor --json)\n          brew uninstall pose\n      - name: Install via WinGet\n        if: runner.os == 'Windows'\n        shell: pwsh\n        # Installing from a local manifest is off by default and has to be\n        # enabled by an administrator; without it winget prints its help and\n        # exits 1, which reads like a usage error rather than a disabled\n        # feature (spec pose-package-channel-install-repair).\n        run: |\n          winget settings --enable LocalManifestFiles\n          # The msstore source demands its own agreements even for an install\n          # that never touches it, and cancels the operation after the download\n          # has already succeeded. This install reads a local manifest, so the\n          # source is removed rather than agreed to.\n          winget source remove --name msstore\n          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { Write-Host \"msstore source already absent\" }\n          $global:LASTEXITCODE = 0\n\n          # Each guarantee is asserted on its own, so a failure names which one\n          # broke rather than surfacing as the step's last exit code.\n          winget validate --manifest .\\package-manifests\\winget\n          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"manifest set failed winget validation\" }\n\n          winget install --manifest .\\package-manifests\\winget --accept-package-agreements --accept-source-agreements --disable-interactivity\n          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"install from the published manifest failed\" }\n\n          # The source checkout's project state is unrelated to the installed\n          # binary and may differ after a Windows checkout. Inspect a fresh\n          # instance created by that binary instead.\n          $smoke = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP \"pose-package-channel-smoke\"\n          New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $smoke | Out-Null\n          git -C $smoke init -q\n          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"could not initialize the smoke repository\" }\n          pose install $smoke --skip-mcp\n          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"the installed binary could not install a fresh instance\" }\n          Push-Location $smoke\n          try {\n            pose doctor --json\n            if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"the installed binary failed doctor in a fresh instance\" }\n          } finally {\n            Pop-Location\n          }\n\n          # Cleanup, not a guarantee: winget does not track an archive package\n          # installed from a local manifest, so neither --id nor --manifest\n          # resolves it afterwards and it reports \"no installed package found\"\n          # straight after a successful install. The runner is ephemeral, so\n          # this is tolerated rather than allowed to fail the channel claim.\n          winget uninstall --manifest .\\package-manifests\\winget --disable-interactivity\n          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { Write-Host \"note: locally-installed archive package is not resolvable for uninstall; skipping cleanup\" }\n          $global:LASTEXITCODE = 0\n","numLines":135,"startLine":1,"totalLines":135}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AztQZt1KVnnk3yULGVVxed","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRHExrgNbAQZj5uCBXT8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KJk55Uk1r1g9BoYAENS28U","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-d0de10e622b0e2942987a4b9c044b402/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5452,"cache_read_input_tokens":90367,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5452},"output_tokens":57,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"3c784d0f-ed34-4f10-a074-906084b1fd23","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:11:36.988Z","request_id":"req_011ChRHExX5hjDLGVSXy5x2N","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KJk55Uk1r1g9BoYAENS28U":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-d0de10e622b0e2942987a4b9c044b402/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KJk55Uk1r1g9BoYAENS28U","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tslug: pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux\n3\tstatus: draft        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\n4\tcreated_at: 2026-11-25\n5\tcompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\n6\tsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\n7\tdepends_on: pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\n8\tremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\n9\tpriority: 3\n10\tcomponents: pose-mcp\n11\ttask_type: feature\n12\tsurface: standard\n13\tdelivers:            # optional typed refs: surface:id, contract:id, capability:id, infrastructure:id, governance:id\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t# Spec: pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux\n17\t\n18\t## 1. Intent\n19\t\n20\t### Goal\n21\tCarry the guarantees `pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes` gives on Linux (through the review run shim) and on Windows (through a job object) to the remaining cases: other Unix platforms, the identities of what Windows and Unix group kills ended, and the environment-search fallback of an embedder without the shim.\n22\t\n23\t### Business value\n24\tReview rounds 13 and 14 of that spec found these gaps; by the maintainer's decision on 2026-11-25 they were moved here so that spec could close on its declared scope (Linux and Windows termination).\n25\t\n26\t### Constraints\n27\tNo new guarantee is claimed before it is enforced and tested on the platform it names.\n28\t\n29\t### Non-goals\n30\tChanging the Linux shim or the Windows job object.\n31\t\n32\t## 2. Requirements\n33\t\n34\t### Functional\n35\t- R1: On Unix platforms other than Linux, after the process-group kill the dispatch shall wait, within a bound, until the group is proven empty, and leave the cleanup incomplete otherwise (round 14, N2).\n36\t- R2: When the Windows job object or a Unix group kill ends processes, the run record shall name them, as the Linux shim's report does (round 14, N3).\n37\t- R3: The environment-search fallback of an embedder without the shim shall not end a process it cannot prove belongs to the run, for example by constraining it to the run's descendants (round 14, N1; limit L6 of the parent spec).\n38\t- R4: Each requirement shall have a test on the platform it concerns, run in CI where that platform is available.\n39\t\n40\t### Non-functional\n41\tExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n42\t\n43\t### Security\n44\tNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n45\t\n46\t### Compatibility\n47\tRecords written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n48\t\n49\t## 3. Technical Plan\n50\t\n51\t### Affected areas\n52\t`pose-mcp` review dispatch, its platform files and the manual.\n53\t\n54\t### Artifacts\n55\tDeclared when the spec starts.\n56\t\n57\t### Delivery targets\n58\tDeclared when the spec starts.\n59\t\n60\t### API/contract changes\n61\tTo be detailed when the spec starts.\n62\t\n63\t### Data/storage changes\n64\tTo be detailed when the spec starts.\n65\t\n66\t### Technical risks\n67\tTo be detailed when the spec starts.\n68\t\n69\t## 4. Tasks\n70\t\n71\t### Planning\n72\t- [ ] Confirm CI availability for macOS and Windows before starting.\n73\t\n74\t### Implementation\n75\t- [ ] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n76\t\n77\t### Validation\n78\t- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n79\t\n80\t## 5. Decisions\n81\t\n82\t## 6. Validation\n83\t\n84\t### Strategy\n85\tEach requirement gets a regression test on its platform.\n86\t\n87\t### Deterministic checks\n88\t\n89\t#### Test\n90\t- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n91\t\n92\t### Execution log\n93\t\n94\t### Results summary\n95\t\n96\t### Requirement trace\n97\t\n98\t### Known gaps\n99\t\n100\t## 7. Final Report\n101\t\n102\t### Delivered scope\n103\t\n104\t### Files and modules changed\n105\t\n106\t### Validation executed\n107\t\n108\t### Residual risks\n109\t\n110\t### Follow-ups\n111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"8f15f035-b8c5-4d18-a4a5-e36da314ec07","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:11:36.994Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-d0de10e622b0e2942987a4b9c044b402/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-25-pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux.md","content":"---\nslug: pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux\nstatus: draft        # draft | in-progress | done | superseded | abandoned; blocked = operational wait, not terminal\ncreated_at: 2026-11-25\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on: pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority: 3\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: feature\nsurface: standard\ndelivers:            # optional typed refs: surface:id, contract:id, capability:id, infrastructure:id, governance:id\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-review-run-reaping-beyond-linux\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nCarry the guarantees `pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes` gives on Linux (through the review run shim) and on Windows (through a job object) to the remaining cases: other Unix platforms, the identities of what Windows and Unix group kills ended, and the environment-search fallback of an embedder without the shim.\n\n### Business value\nReview rounds 13 and 14 of that spec found these gaps; by the maintainer's decision on 2026-11-25 they were moved here so that spec could close on its declared scope (Linux and Windows termination).\n\n### Constraints\nNo new guarantee is claimed before it is enforced and tested on the platform it names.\n\n### Non-goals\nChanging the Linux shim or the Windows job object.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: On Unix platforms other than Linux, after the process-group kill the dispatch shall wait, within a bound, until the group is proven empty, and leave the cleanup incomplete otherwise (round 14, N2).\n- R2: When the Windows job object or a Unix group kill ends processes, the run record shall name them, as the Linux shim's report does (round 14, N3).\n- R3: The environment-search fallback of an embedder without the shim shall not end a process it cannot prove belongs to the run, for example by constraining it to the run's descendants (round 14, N1; limit L6 of the parent spec).\n- R4: Each requirement shall have a test on the platform it concerns, run in CI where that platform is available.\n\n### Non-functional\nExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n\n### Security\nNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n\n### Compatibility\nRecords written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n`pose-mcp` review dispatch, its platform files and the manual.\n\n### Artifacts\nDeclared when the spec starts.\n\n### Delivery targets\nDeclared when the spec starts.\n\n### API/contract changes\nTo be detailed when the spec starts.\n\n### Data/storage changes\nTo be detailed when the spec starts.\n\n### Technical risks\nTo be detailed when the spec starts.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Planning\n- [ ] Confirm CI availability for macOS and Windows before starting.\n\n### Implementation\n- [ ] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n\n### Validation\n- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nEach requirement gets a regression test on its platform.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Execution log\n\n### Results summary\n\n### Requirement trace\n\n### Known gaps\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\n\n### Files and modules changed\n\n### Validation executed\n\n### Residual risks\n\n### Follow-ups\n","numLines":111,"startLine":1,"totalLines":111}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KJk55Uk1r1g9BoYAENS28U","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
