{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRHJNxLipCGUoFMU59d2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"decision: approved\n\n**This round could not run any command, so POSE will probably refuse this approval.** All Bash calls failed with `Sandbox is required but failed to initialize: Failed to create bridge sockets after 5 attempts`.\n\n- **Not run:** no tests, `go vet`, `git diff` or planned `pose` tool ran, and `review draft-check` did not check this draft.\n- **Cleanup failed:** the final `go clean -cache` and `go-build*` removal command did not run, so no cleanup happened.\n- **Required tools:** they are marked `deferred`. POSE requires `passed` for required tools, so it is likely to reject the draft. I did not claim runs that didn't happen.\n- **Basis for the decision:** I read the current files and relied on the sealed evidence. Without a diff, I located the changed code from the spec and by search.\n- **Before the next round:** fix the sandbox startup. Round 1 reportedly failed the same way.\n\n## Result\n\nI found no blocking defect in the code. R1–R3 hold on reading:\n\n- **Stable path (R1):** each attempt gets `pose-review-run-<32 hex>` under the temporary directory (`review_dispatch.go:2049-2070`). Attempt IDs include a random nonce, so separate attempts get separate paths.\n- **Exclusive creation (R3):** `os.Mkdir` refuses existing paths and links. Both planners check the path (`review_run_continuity.go:431`, `delegation_handoff.go:347`) before the claim at `review_dispatch.go:746`. The exclusive claim comes before directory creation, so two continuations don't share a directory.\n- **Cleanup:** it still removes the whole runtime directory (`review_adapter_containment.go:510-631`). A failure right after creation removes the empty directory.\n- **Regression test (R2):** by reading, it would fail with random names. I did not run it or any mutation.\n\n## Previous findings\n\n| Finding | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| R2-N6 | fixed | Handoff checks the directory before claiming |\n| R2-N7 | fixed | Four manuals, spec line 80 and the refusal message are corrected |\n| R2-N8 | partial | Message and spec follow-up updated; the race remains (N12) |\n| R2-N9 | fixed | Both tests match the `RunContinuity` pattern |\n| R2-N10 | fixed | `TMPDIR`, `TMP` and `TEMP` are all set |\n\n## Findings (all low, follow-up)\n\n- **N11** `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:2049`: a run interrupted under an earlier engine used a random path. Resuming it now creates the stable path, so the session meets the old failure without being told. The manual's \"every run of an attempt\" doesn't hold for these runs.\n- **N12** `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go:431`: this carries R2-N8. A concurrent resume that loses the race can be told to remove a live run's directory instead of getting `pending`.\n- **N13** `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:2082`: a refused handoff tells the operator to \"then resume\", though they asked for a handoff.\n- **N14** `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go:32`: on Windows without symlink privilege, the test fails instead of skipping. I found no workflow that runs it on Windows.\n- **N15** `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go:699`: a session continued into a new round gets a different checkout path from the one it saw. This is outside this spec, which covers resume.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"N11\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\", \"line\": 2049, \"summary\": \"A run interrupted under an earlier engine used a random runtime directory; resuming it creates the stable path, so the session still points at the removed checkout and is not told. The predecessor's recorded safety.runtime_id could detect this.\", \"action\": \"Detect a predecessor whose runtime_id differs from the attempt's stable name and refuse or document the transition.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-26\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N12\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\", \"line\": 431, \"summary\": \"Carries R2-N8: the claim lookup and directory check are not atomic, so a resume that loses a race can get the directory refusal instead of pending. The message now warns that a run may be starting. Established by reading.\", \"action\": \"Make the claim lookup and directory check one step, or re-read the claim before refusing.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-26\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N13\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\", \"line\": 2082, \"summary\": \"PlanReviewHandoff returns the same refusal as resume, which ends with 'then resume' although the operator asked for a handoff.\", \"action\": \"Word the remedy as 'then run the command again' or per caller.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-26\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N14\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\", \"line\": 32, \"summary\": \"os.Symlink failure is fatal, so the test fails on Windows without symlink privilege instead of skipping the link case.\", \"action\": \"Skip the link case when the platform refuses to create a symlink.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-26\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N15\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\", \"line\": 699, \"summary\": \"A session continued into a new round belongs to a new attempt, so its checkout path differs from the one the session saw. Outside this spec's resume scope; established by reading.\", \"action\": \"Decide whether a continued round should be told its new checkout path.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-26\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R2-N6\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go:347 calls reviewRunRuntimeDirFree during planning, before the claim at review_dispatch.go:746; review_run_continuity_test.go:323-327 covers it. Read, not run.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R2-N7\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"POSE.md:1045, locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1042, scaffold/dist/POSE.md:1032, scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1042, spec line 80 and review_dispatch.go:2082 limit the removal remedy to a directory present after a clean run and say incomplete cleanup is not resumed (review_run_continuity.go:405).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R2-N8\", \"status\": \"partial\", \"evidence\": \"review_dispatch.go:2082 now mentions a starting run and spec line 140 records the follow-up; the non-atomic check at review_run_continuity.go:413-431 remains (N12).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R2-N9\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"review_run_continuity_test.go:299 and review_run_runtime_dir_test.go:13 are named TestRunContinuity..., matched by the RunContinuity pattern at .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json:2639.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R2-N10\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"review_run_runtime_dir_test.go:16-19 sets TMPDIR, TMP and TEMP to a test directory.\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Read-only sweep, no commands could run: the spec; runtime directory creation, check, use and cleanup; dispatch, resume and handoff planning and claim ordering; attempt identity; resume, handoff and next-action CLI callers; both changed tests; the validation matrix entry; the manual paragraph in four copies; round thread continuation; accepted limits L1-L3. No git diff was available.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the assumptions of a stable TMPDIR (L1), a predictable path (L2) and escaped processes (L3). Exclusive creation was verified by reading. The unstated assumption about earlier-engine runs is N11. L3's cited follow-up spec is still a draft and its requirements are narrower than the wording suggests; the same-user argument is what supports the limit.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Run record fields are unchanged; runtime_id keeps holding the directory base name; runs without an attempt keep random names and tasks use another path. The transition for earlier interrupted runs is N11, no worse than before.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The cause is a resumed session pointing at a removed random path. A per-attempt path recreates it, and D1 keeps the sealed brief and its wire digest unchanged.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Read the resume paragraph in both locales and both scaffold copies; it matches the code for runs of this engine, including TMPDIR, refusal before claim and incomplete cleanup.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Refusals name the directory and the remedy and reach next actions. Wording and race gaps are N12 and N13.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The code read covers only the runtime directory, its pre-claim check, tests and manual text named in the spec; no diff could be run to exclude other edits beyond the sealed change list.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"os.Mkdir with 0700 neither follows links nor reuses a path; cleanup still checks directory identity; the predictable path risks fall within L2 and L3.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"A derived path and one existence check is smaller than telling the session a new path, which would change verified input. It stops holding if TMPDIR changes (L1).\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Attempted; the Bash sandbox failed to start (bridge sockets).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Bash sandbox unavailable.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Bash sandbox unavailable.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"asses